# MUnit Testing Standards

## Test Suite Organization
- One test suite per Mule flow file (one-to-one correlation)
- Test suites are located under `src/test/munit/`
- Test resource files (payloads, assertions) go under `src/test/resources/`

## Minimum Coverage
- **At least 70% code coverage** per test suite
- **At least 70% overall coverage** when all suites are run together
- Account for processors imported from shared libraries (may not be coverable)

## Required Test Cases
- Each flow must have **at least one positive test** (happy path)
- Each flow must have **at least one negative test** (error handling path)
- Test both success responses and error responses for each endpoint

## Mocking
- All calls to backend/external resources **must be mocked**
- Never make real HTTP calls or database queries in unit tests
- Use MUnit mocks for HTTP Request, Database, Salesforce, Anypoint MQ connectors

## Test Naming
- Follow the same naming conventions as implementation flows
- Test names should clearly indicate what is being tested and the expected outcome
- Example: `post:\addressValidation:application\json:na-sf-exp-api-config-test-error`

## Test Data
- Use per-endpoint folders for test event data (payload, attributes, variables)
- DWL files for setting event data: `set-event_payload.dwl`, `set-event_attributes.dwl`
- DWL files for assertions: `assert_expression_payload.dwl`
- JSON fixtures for mock responses in their own folders

## Pre-Commit Verification
- Run `mvn clean test -P<profile>` from command line before committing
- All test suites must pass with 100% success rate

## Review Checklist
- [ ] At least one positive and one negative test per flow
- [ ] All external calls are mocked
- [ ] Code coverage meets 70% minimum threshold
- [ ] Test data is organized in per-endpoint folders
- [ ] Tests pass via `mvn clean test`
